# RRF macro line length (hard stop)

RepRapFirmware fails boot/config with **`GCode command too long`** when a single macro line is too long. That prevents `nxt.g` from finishing and leaves **`global.nxtLoaded` false**.

## Rules for every agent (mandatory)

1. **Maximum 200 characters** per line in any `macros/**/*.g` file (full line, including indentation). Comment-only lines (`;`) are exempt.
2. **Do not** write long compound `if { ... }` on one line. Split into `var` booleans, then a short `if { var.name }`.
3. **Do not** write long `echo`, `abort`, or `M291 P{...}` on one line. Assign message parts to `var` first.
4. **Before** claiming macro work is done, run: `node dist/check-gcode-line-length.mjs` — must exit 0.
5. If the checker fails, **fix all reported lines** in the same task. Do not commit, build a plugin ZIP, or tag until it passes.
6. Read [docs/RRF_LINE_LENGTH.md](../../docs/RRF_LINE_LENGTH.md) when editing boot path (`nxt.g`, `nxt-boot.g`, `config.g` callers) or migration/import macros.

## Example pattern (required for complex conditions)

```gcode
var nxtCondA = { ... }
var nxtCondB = { ... }
var nxtDoThing = { var.nxtCondA || var.nxtCondB }
if { var.nxtDoThing }
    M98 P"other.g"
```

Never ship a one-line version of `nxtDoThing` if it would exceed 200 characters.
